body:
Xmage uses multiple AI classes (#10154):
* `HumanPlayer` for real games;
* `TestPlayer` for unit tests;
* `ComputerPlayer` for direct choices, e.g. on resolve or card picks (it also used in unit tests with non-strict mode);
* `ComputerPlayer7` for priority simulations;

`ComputerPlayer`'s code is bloated and full of hacks. Also it used many workaround with target's filters and direct permanent searching/adding -- dozens of `instanceOf TargetXXX`, unsupported targets, etc.

Now it use a shared and a **simple cards and targets selection logic due effect's outcome and possible targets priority** (see `PossibleTargetsSelector`):
- for good effects:
  - choose itself and own objects as much as possible (biggest creatures first);
  - choose opponent and opponent's objects as low as possible (worst creatures first);
- for bad effects:
  - choose itself and own objects as low as possible (worst creatures first);
  - choose opponent and opponent's objects as much as possible (biggest creatures first);
- planeswalkers/battles are most priority targets, all other sorted due battlefield score (see `GameStateEvaluator2` - it's part of current `ComputerPlayer7` and game simulations);

For **DEVS** -- you must use that logic for outcome:
- if player must choose card/permanent and do a bad things with it -- set bad outcome;
- if player must choose card/permanent and do a good things with it -- set good outcome;
- for custom and complex effects call choose dialogs with specific `Outcome.XXX` -- do not use default `outcome` field (that's field used for targets selection before cast/activate/play);

That's logic already used in some choices like `chooseTarget(target)`, but now it improved and used all around. Mulligans, card picks, declare attackers/blockers still use own logic. Some non-strict tests were affected but that's ok. There are known problems with complex targets like multiple zones selection -- but it can't be fixed without game simulations.

Details changes:
- ai: removed outdated/unused code from AI, battlefield score, targeting, etc;
- ai: removed all targeting and filters related logic from ComputerPlayer;
- ai: improved targeting with shared and simple logic due effect's outcome and possible targets priority;
- ai: improved get amount selection (now AI will not choose big and useless values);
- ai: improved spell selection on free cast (now AI will try to cast spells with valid targets only);
- tests: improved result table with first bad dialog info for fast access (part of #13638);

P.S. Related and closed issues will be added later
